Aim:
To handle exceptions in PL/SQL.

Algorithm:
1. Declare two variables.
2. Perform division.
3. Handle division-by-zero errors.
4. Display the result or error message.

Program:
SET SERVEROUTPUT ON;

DECLARE
    A NUMBER := 10;
    B NUMBER := 0;
    C NUMBER;
BEGIN
    C := A / B;
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Result = ' || C);

EXCEPTION
    WHEN ZERO_DIVIDE THEN
        DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Error: Division by zero');


    WHEN OTHERS THEN
        DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Some other error occurred');
END;
/

Result:
The exception was handled successfully without an unhandled program termination.
/
